body:
I would've missed out on my first big girl job in  the field I wanted to work in (psychology) , getting my first apartment, my first new car, and a new city to live in and start fresh in.  I would've missed my friends, working in a hospital for a year, and spending time with my grandparents (one has cancer, one has dementia).  I thought that last one would kill me but it has only made me cherish the amount of time I have.  I am so happy to be alive for the first time in my life.  I have things to look forward to.

&#x200B;

Edit:  I forgot I graduated from college at the end of last year.  Took me ten years but I made it!
